{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>בר</b> — it is what is clean from chaff, like the pattern of חג פת בג." "<b>יקבוהו</b> — from the matter of קבה לי, and its root, for the pattern of קבה is הבה, and likewise ארה לי. The parallel among them: נקבה יהבה נארה שמעה סלחה." "<b>משביר</b> — one who sells grain. The meaning: one who withholds his produce in a time of famine until he sells it at dear prices — peoples will curse him, and blessing will come upon the head of one who sells his grain in a time of need."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:14.432209047Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}